# Cursor Rules for LeechBot

## Overview
LeechBot — Pyrogram 2.0.106 Telegram bot for file transloading. Python 3.10+, asyncio.

## Code Style
- Async/await everywhere (asyncio application)
- `logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)` at module top
- Standard file header block (project, developer, license)
- No linter configured — follow existing patterns
- Type hints on function signatures preferred but not required
- Direct state mutation via `leechbot/utility/variables.py` classes

## Key Imports
```python
from leechbot import app, OWNER, DUMP_ID
from leechbot.utility.variables import BOT, MSG, Transfer, BotTimes, Messages, Paths
from leechbot.utility.helper import sizeUnit, status_bar, keyboard, sysINFO
```

## Commands
Handlers in `leechbot/commands.py`:
```python
@app.on_message(filters.command("cmdname"))
async def handler(client, message):
    ...
```

## Callbacks
All in `leechbot/callbacks.py`:
```python
@app.on_callback_query()
async def handle_callback(client, callback_query):
    data = callback_query.data
    if data == "action": ...
```

## Downloaders
- One file per source in `leechbot/downloader/`
- Link detection patterns in `leechbot/utility/helper.py`
- Routing in `leechbot/downloader/manager.py`

## Upload
- `upload_file(file_path, real_name)` — single file with progress
- `upload_photos_batch(photo_paths, remove)` — batch via file_id grouping
- `reply_media_group()` does NOT support progress — use per-photo upload workaround

## State
All mutable state in `leechbot/utility/variables.py`:
- `BOT.Setting` — persistent preferences
- `BOT.Options` — per-task options (reset each task)
- `BOT.Mode` — current task mode
- `BOT.State` — control flags
- `Queue` — download queue (deque)
- `Transfer` — file transfer stats
- `BotStats` — cumulative stats

## Constraints
- Pyrogram 2.0.106: no `style` on buttons, no `progress` on media groups
- Telegram 2GB limit, media group max 10
- No test suite — test manually
- Changelog: every change adds entry at top of `CHANGELOG.md`

## Files to Read First
1. `AGENTS.md` — full agent instructions
2. `ARCHITECTURE.md` — technical deep dive
3. `config.py` — all configuration
4. `leechbot/utility/variables.py` — all state
